m/users/peteski/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-05T21:43:22Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T21:43:22Z","body":"All good, I have someone who can help me, I'll give it a try today and get back to you.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6003600975/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6027149034","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124175#issuecomment-6027149034","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124175","id":6027149034,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZz7-6g","user":{"login":"peteski","id":3522412,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjI0MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3522412?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski","html_url":"https://github.com/peteski","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T23:12:44Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T23:27:34Z","body":"Hey, I tried that out and it still seems to be having your issue of snapping back. \r\nCan I ask, are you using \"Maya Navigation Scheme\" ?\r\n\r\nI had some success fixing my problem (and maybe yours), if you comment out line 111 of view_3d_controller.cpp\r\n`//cancel_navigation();`\r\nIt stops it from messing with the view and works great again :) \r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6027149034/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6047340653","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124175#issuecomment-6047340653","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124175","id":6047340653,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaHMYbQ","user":{"login":"Image-unavailable","id":56268917,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MjY4OTE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56268917?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable","html_url":"https://github.com/Image-unavailable","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-07T21:36:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-07T21:38:11Z","body":"> Hey, I tried that out and it still seems to be having your issue of snapping back.\r\n\r\nBy \"issue of snapping back\" do you mean that the camera snaps back when pressing the right mouse button while another mouse button is held? Or that the camera snaps back when pressing the right mouse button *even when no mouse button is held*?\r\n\r\nThis PR is meant to fix only the second case. This is because that specific behaviour is a bug (specifically a regression, AKA a \"this worked in an old version but it's broken in the new one\" bug), and regression bugfixes are generally uncontroversial.\r\n\r\nHowever, if it's the first case, pressing the right mouse button to reset camera position is a new feature added in #105791, which means maintainers basically said \"yeah we want this thing, we think it's useful\".\r\n\r\n> I had some success fixing my problem (and maybe yours), if you comment out line 111 of view_3d_controller.cpp `//cancel_navigation();`\r\n\r\nYeah, that's why I'm asking if it's the first or second case. Removing the RMB-reset should be easy to do by reverting #105791 outright, but as maintainers *intentionally* added it (that is, it's not a bug), if you have issues with what the PR added you basically have to say that you want a way to turn it off, and explain why that is the case (and *not* by saying that it's bug, because it isn't one).\r\n\r\nAs for myself, I use the Godot navigation scheme. But I tested the Maya scheme, and it seems to work properly with this bugfix PR in place. However, you have to pay attention not to overlap inputs, so for example if you want to transition from a pan to a zoom, you have to release the middle mouse button before pressing the right mouse button to zoom, or it will reset camera position (as intended).\r\n\r\nPerhaps this isn't as smooth as in older versions, but it seems reasonable to me to release buttons when transitioning from one action to another? Even though this wasn't necessary in older versions. Of course, your opinion on this may be different.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6047340653/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6048434068","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124175#issuecomment-6048434068","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124175","id":6048434068,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaIPHlA","user":{"login":"peteski","id":3522412,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjI0MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3522412?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski","html_url":"https://github.com/peteski","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peteski/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-07T22:48:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-07T22:48:35Z","body":"Ahhh haha! Sorry, I got that compl